// if a language wants to be any level of successful past being used
//  it must include some way of interacting with other languages
//  especially c libraries

// some things are made to help with interop at a language level
// e.g. strings should include a null at the end of data
//  and so string.data can be used as an input to char*


// I think JAIs first metaprogram that can interface with the compiler is a cool idea
//  and this is where adding libraries would happen
ws.add_library("raylib")

